  "summary": "The paper studies a variational quantum circuit fraud-detection model on reduced Intesa Sanpaolo transaction datasets of 1,000 to 20,000 samples and 2, 4, 6, or 8 PCA features, using PennyLane default.qubit for training and IBM Brisbane/Algiers for noise checks. The main reported result is that VQC variants can outperform classical baselines on precision/recall for some reduced datasets, but real-device noise severely degrades performance and no practical quantum advantage is demonstrated.",
